cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Scholastic: an open research workspace with enforced attribution"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Karat
    given-names: Gautam
repository-code: "https://github.com/novicecoder10/scholastic"
abstract: >-
  A self-hostable scholarly research workspace: federated search across nine
  open sources with deduplication and ranking, a PDF reader whose assistant
  answers with page-level citations, an evidence matrix in which every filled
  cell retains the page and sentence it was extracted from, and manuscript and
  slide-deck writers that delete any generated claim they cannot attribute to a
  supplied source. AI capacity is allocated through a credit commons whose
  credits are never purchasable and never transferable.
keywords:
  - literature search
  - open science
  - scholarly communication
  - systematic review
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - research software
license: MIT
version: 0.5.0
date-released: "2026-09-08"
